course: dictionary
lesson: 9045
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. A dictionary lists each meaning with a number, so you need the sentence around the word to pick the right one. «Sledding is safest feet first, sitting up, on a hill away from roads, trees and ponds.» Here sledding means riding down a snowy hill on a sled.
explain: Sledding is a noun for the activity. It has no plural, so you never say sleddings. It comes from the verb sled, which you can use as «I sled down the hill» or «I was sledding all afternoon».
explain: The American phrase «tough sledding» has nothing to do with snow. It means progress is hard. To check, swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense. The snow meaning would not fit a sentence about a hard project, but the hard progress meaning would.
fact: Sledding means riding down a snowy hill on a sled, which is also called a sledge.
fact: Sledding has no plural, so it is never «sleddings».
fact: In American informal use, «tough sledding» means progress is hard or slow.
fact: Sledding is safest feet first, sitting up, on a hill with no trees, rocks, roads or water at the bottom. Wear a helmet, and never sled on frozen ponds.
fact: Sleds slide because snow and ice have little friction, and gravity pulls them down the slope.
exercise: «Sledding head first makes head and neck injuries more likely.» What is the safest way to go sledding? | Head first, to go faster | *Feet first, sitting up | Lying flat with your head at the front | Standing up with your head forward
exercise: Priya says, «Our science project was tough sledding.» What does tough sledding mean? | The snow was deep on the hill | *Making progress was hard | We went down the hill very fast | The sled was broken
exercise: «Sledding is done on a hill away from roads, trees and ponds.» Why must the hill be away from roads? | So the sled stays dry | Roads are good for sleds | So the sled can go faster | *So the sledder does not crash into things
test: Sledding is a favourite winter game. What is sledding? | *Riding down a snowy hill on a sled | Skating on a frozen pond | Walking up a hill with a sled | Making a snowman in the garden
test: Dad says, «Writing this report is tough sledding.» Does he mean the report is easy? | No, it is about snow | *No, it is hard going | Yes, it is fun to do | Yes, it is quick and simple
exam: Which meaning of «tough sledding» fits a story about a hard maths test? | Riding on a sled down a hill | A safe hill with no trees | Snowy weather | *Hard progress
